# Goal

Integrate the DroneRF dataset into the NoisyUAV signal processing pipeline. Specifically, design a data loader that interprets DroneRF's custom format and seamlessly feeds it into the `detectar_bursts` function (Stage 1 Entropy Detector) ensuring identical performance as the Jupyter notebook.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The DroneRF dataset recorded the RF environment using two synchronous SDRs, splitting an 80 MHz bandwidth into two 40 MHz files: `L` (Low) and `H` (High). 
> **How to treat these bands?** Since our `detectar_bursts` and CNN are trained strictly on a 14 MHz scale, I propose that we build our loader to pick ONE of the bands (`L` or `H`) and mathematically **downsample (diezmar) it from 40 MHz to 14 MHz** using `scipy.signal.resample`. This simulates having tuned our 14 MHz SDR into either the upper or lower half of the 2.4 GHz band. Are you okay with treating `H` and `L` as independent channels and decimating them?

